title: The Reform Slate
subtitle: Ten years buys three fights. Choose which ones.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_major_reform_card
frequency: 320
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and reform_slate_closed = 0 and reform_pressure_pending = 0 and poland_reform_slate_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.poland_reform_slate_timer = 2;
// A slate pick is a judgement about terrain, so the card reads the public-mood
// model out loud instead of making the player guess which fields are winnable.
const slateIssues = {
    abortion: "abortion_rights",
    marriage: "lgbt_equality",
    church: "secular_state",
    asylum: "refugee_solidarity",
    border: "border_security",
    defence: "national_security",
    labor: "social_spending",
    health: "vaccination",
    courts: "rule_of_law"
};
for (const issue of Object.keys(slateIssues)) {
    const field = slateIssues[issue];
    const support = Math.round(Number(Q[field + "_support"]) || 0);
    const salience = Math.round(Number(Q[field + "_salience"]) || 0);
    const backlash = Math.round(Number(Q[field + "_backlash"]) || 0);
    const verdict = support >= 60
        ? "a broad mandate is available"
        : (support >= 52
            ? "favourable terrain"
            : (support >= 45
                ? "closely contested"
                : (support >= 38
                    ? "difficult terrain"
                    : "the country is against us")));
    const heat = salience >= 60
        ? "high salience"
        : (salience >= 40 ? "active concern" : "low attention");
    const opposition = backlash >= 60
        ? "polarised"
        : (backlash >= 45 ? "organised opposition" : "limited backlash");
    Q["slate_" + issue + "_climate"] =
        verdict + " · " + heat + " · " + opposition +
        " (support " + support + ", attention " + salience +
        ", backlash " + backlash + ")";
}
!}
card-image: img/poland/cards/programme-convention.webp

= What is this decade actually for?

**Slate: [+ reform_slate_count +] of [+ reform_slate_max +] chosen · [+
reform_slate_slots_left +] left.**

A governing party can carry three defining reforms across ten years. Not nine.
Every field below has a settlement ladder of four tiers, a public climate that
prices resistance, and veto players who will not all be moved by the same
argument.

A pick is permanent. The slate cannot be reopened once it is full, and a
settlement — even a humiliating one — closes that field for the rest of the
campaign.

[? if reform_slate_slots_left = 1: This is the last slot. Choosing it closes the
programme for the decade.?]

- @pick_abortion
- @pick_marriage
- @pick_church
- @pick_asylum
- @pick_border
- @pick_defence
- @pick_labor
- @pick_health
- @pick_courts
- @defer

@pick_abortion
title: Reproductive rights
subtitle: [+ slate_abortion_climate +]
view-if: abortion_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: abortion_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names reproductive rights as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: emergency decriminalisation, a limited compromise, legal access through
twelve weeks, the Canadian model. A right-wing Palace will not sign above the
first rung at any price.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_marriage
title: Legal recognition and equal marriage
subtitle: [+ slate_marriage_climate +]
view-if: marriage_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: marriage_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names equal marriage as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: a closest-person agreement, registered cohabitation, civil partnerships,
marriage equality with adoption. KO is lukewarm rather than hostile; PSL's
conservatives are the arithmetic problem.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_church
title: Church, school and the secular state
subtitle: [+ slate_church_climate +]
view-if: church_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: church_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names the concordat settlement as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: catechism funding moved off the school budget, religion out of the
timetable, the Church Fund abolished, concordat renegotiation. The treaty tier
needs a Palace that will sign against the episcopate.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_asylum
title: Asylum and refugee reception
subtitle: [+ slate_asylum_climate +]
view-if: asylum_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: asylum_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names asylum reform as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: humanitarian access, a lawful procedure with legal aid, reception
capacity and work rights, a European solidarity settlement. The hardest field in
the game: the public is against us and no partner gains from helping.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_border
title: The eastern-border regime
subtitle: [+ slate_border_climate +]
view-if: border_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: border_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names the border regime as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: a statutory footing for the emergency, civilian oversight, a funded
technical border, a lawful audited service under civilian command. Broadly
popular; the resistance is institutional rather than electoral.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_defence
title: Defence and allied security
subtitle: [+ slate_defence_climate +]
view-if: defence_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: defence_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names the defence settlement as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: an audited procurement pipeline, conscript-free readiness and veteran
provision, domestic industrial production, a civilian-controlled settlement with
European integration. The one field where the Palace is usually an ally.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_labor
title: Labour-law reconstruction
subtitle: [+ slate_labor_climate +]
view-if: labor_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: labor_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names labour-law reconstruction as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: funded inspection, PIP powers, contract and labour-law protections, the
full Razem package. Popular in the country and cold inside any KO-led cabinet.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_health
title: Public health service reconstruction
subtitle: [+ slate_health_climate +]
view-if: health_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: health_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names health reconstruction as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: emergency staffing money, a funded primary and psychiatric network,
public financing raised and private lanes closed, a rebuilt universal service.
Everyone agrees about the queue and not about the answer.

- #poland_card_finish

@pick_courts
title: Rule-of-law repair
subtitle: [+ slate_courts_climate +]
view-if: courts_on_slate = 0
on-arrival: courts_on_slate = 1; news_headline = "Lewica names rule-of-law repair as a defining reform of the decade"

Ladder: neo-judge status case by case, a lawful KRS, Constitutional Tribunal
repair, a complete constitutional reset. The cheapest reform to pass with KO and
the easiest to pass badly.

- #poland_card_finish

@defer
title: Do not commit yet — keep every field open
subtitle: Free. The slate stays open; the card returns in two months.
on-arrival: news_headline = "Lewica postpones naming its defining reforms"

Waiting is not free in a ten-year campaign, but committing to a field whose
public climate is still moving is worse. The programme convention can name its
fights later.

- #poland_card_finish
